# Keep line endings LF everywhere, including on a Windows checkout.
#
# The typegen and generate suites compare their output against golden files
# byte for byte. Git's default autocrlf on Windows rewrites those files to CRLF
# on checkout, so every one of them fails on the first line -- a diff that
# looks like a real behaviour difference and is not. The CLI also writes LF on
# every platform, so a CRLF golden file would be wrong even if the test
# tolerated it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
